@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# POSTING: isolated read-only cut
+
+Base: `66047c25fee1f8e9700620e906cb07b0ac82dabe`, with the same tree as
+`381ae4da339dc9bc7f3edbdac2c8011bee000693`. This is not an activated branch.
+
+## Ownership blocker and passive contract
+
+The concrete coordinator mappings exist only in `server/posting-registry.ts`.
+They establish identity assertions, not ownership or runtime connection.
+Existing BlackRoom configuration and its singleton gate do not provide a
+persisted source/physical-account relationship to a proven request owner.
+`server/single-user-owner.ts` accepts configured/local owner IDs or a username;
+this is deliberately NOT used to attach these identities to authenticated users.
+The Clipper/global metadata and growth-scout readers do not supply the missing
+owner/source proof either.
+
+Consequently the production reader performs no IO and returns
+`owner_source_binding_unproven` and no accounts, for every authenticated caller.
+The endpoint requires the existing request identity resolver, denies conflicting
+owner queries before calling the reader, and never reads identity proofs from
+HTTP body/query. No new store, table, default dataset, connection, permission,
+credential, provider request or discovery/refresh is introduced.
+
+The pure adapter contract accepts only proofs of existing owner-bound source
+records supplied by a future separately reviewed passive reader. The current
+adapter cannot produce them. Positive tests use synthetic owner/source proofs,
+not real users, source data or an attestation available to browsers.
+
+## Identity and privacy
+
+Canonical identities are platform + verified native ID, otherwise a verified
+handle with supported platform semantics. Metricool blog references are aliases
+only. TikTok handles case-fold; numeric IDs remain decimal strings. Facebook
+usernames ignore periods/case and numeric IDs take priority. YouTube channel
+IDs are case-sensitive; handle-only Unicode semantics remain unsupported,
+therefore unavailable. Conflicting proofs fail closed rather than merging.
+Platform + Metricool alias resolving to multiple physical identities is also a
+veto, never a replacement for the platform + physical-identity dedup key.
+
+Only owned records contribute to accounts, aliases or excluded counts. Unknown
+owners/sources are unavailable, not a verified empty inventory. Missing Facebook
+identity remains unknown. A physical KONG TikTok identity has one canonical
+record despite its two Metricool references. Supplied identities are never
+advertised as runtime-connected, publishing or learning.
+
+The client verifies auth owner before its sole new passive request, requires an
+exact response owner, strips non-public fields, rejects oversize/malformed data,
+keeps canonical identity keys, and clears prior-owner state on change/denial.
+Concrete mappings are not embedded in the client or shared runtime modules.
+
+## Product scope
+
+Online-only department cards separate roles/responsible parties, accounts,
+style, material, calendar and metrics. KONG is TikTok party/experience content;
+Black Room is DJ sets/clips with a distinct style. News/clipping and future
+brands stay proposals when evidence is absent. Marketing research/outreach,
+responses and follow-up towards KONG downloads are disconnected proposals.
+The claimed DJ list on an offline Mac is not accessed/imported; no leads/emails
+or sends. Growth Scout stays pending because passive ownership is unproven.
+Costs are informative, not zero-cost or paid-LLM-per-lead promises.
+
+## Validation and review
+
+Pure unit/auth/transport tests use fixtures and zero provider IO. The browser
+harness mounts the real Agents Office page and CompanyOffice with every request
+intercepted, using an existing installed Chromium, no HTTP listener or app
+startup. Build checkpoints precede both harness compilation and the safe
+client-only build. Logs retain exit codes. No full deployment build, backend
+startup, real DB, provider, workflow, installation, activation or publication.
